{"name":"Millennial Greige","hex":"#939796","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"millennial","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Thousand-year-old; also  thousands of years old.","Occurring every thousand years."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Often capitalized: a person from the generation born in the last two decades of the 20th century, from around the early 1980s to the mid-1990s and who reached adulthood early in the third millennium C.E., characterized by their familiarity with computer technology and poorer financial prospects than their parents.","A thousandth anniversary; also, a celebration of such an anniversary."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/millennial"},{"term":"greige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of clothing, textiles, etc.: neither bleached nor dyed, nor otherwise fully processed; unfinished.","Of a colour like that of unbleached or undyed fabric, between grey and beige."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of unbleached or undyed fabric between grey and beige, closely akin to taupe.","Clothing, textiles, etc., which have neither been bleached nor dyed, nor otherwise fully processed; greige goods."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greige"}],"entries":[{"title":"Millennials","blocks":[{"text":"Millennials, also known as Generation Y or Gen Y, are the demographic cohort following Generation X and preceding Generation Z. Researchers and popular media use the early 1980s as starting birth years and the mid-1990s to early 2000s as ending birth years, with the generation typically being defined as people born from 1981 to 1996. Most millennials are the children of baby boomers and older Gen Xers, and are often the parents of younger Generation Z and Generation Alpha."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Generation_timeline_simple.svg/330px-Generation_timeline_simple.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millennials","wikidata":"Q277633"},{"title":"Greige goods","blocks":[{"text":"Greige goods are loom state woven fabrics, or unprocessed knitted fabrics. Greige goods undergo many subsequent processes, for instance, dyeing, printing, bleaching, and finishing, prior to further converting to finished goods such as clothing, or other textile products. \"Grey fabrics\" is another term to refer to unfinished woven or knitted fabrics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Rolls_of_dressed_fibre._Silk_industry_%28spun_silk%29%2C_South_Manchester%2C_Conn.%2C_U.S.A_%28NYPL_b11707678-G90F070_013F%29.tiff/lossy-page1-330px-Rolls_of_dressed_fibre._Silk_industry_%28spun_silk%29%2C_South_Manchester%2C_Conn.%2C_U.S.A_%28NYPL_b11707678-G90F070_013F%29.tiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greige_goods","wikidata":"Q105985607"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg/500px-Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg/1280px-Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg/500px-Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Linkin Park was a popular music group among millennials[119]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALinkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Future_Music_Festival_2011_%285520592096%29.jpg/500px-Future_Music_Festival_2011_%285520592096%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&